* Reference solution: current-biased Sky130 five-transistor OTA.
* XM1-XM5 form the signal core; XM6 is the diode-connected bias replica.
* NMOS input pair (L = 0.9 um) and PMOS mirror load (W = 100 um, L = 0.9 um): the wide load keeps
* its source-gate drop low, so at 1.62 V and -40 C the pair and the tail still have the drain
* headroom to stay saturated, which common-mode and supply rejection need.
* 3.3:1 tail mirror at L = 1.5 um sets about 167 uA nominal tail current within the 0.5 mW budget.
.subckt ota_5t vss ibias vdd vinn vinp vout
XM1 nleft vinp tail vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.9 w=90 nf=10
XM2 vout vinn tail vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.9 w=90 nf=10
XM3 nleft nleft vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 l=0.9 w=100 nf=20
XM4 vout nleft vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 l=0.9 w=100 nf=20
XM5 tail ibias vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=1.5 w=300 nf=30
XM6 ibias ibias vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=1.5 w=90 nf=9
.ends ota_5t
